Changes from the reference implementation

The YSM container parsing, format-specific decryption/decompression and
geometry reconstruction have been ported to Java 21. The implementation
uses JCA/JDK facilities, zstd-jni and Java ImageIO providers in place of
corresponding C++ facilities. The Java project adds in-memory InputStream,
byte[] and Path APIs, structured warnings, checked extraction paths,
Blockbench project reconstruction, embedded textures and texture fallback,
animation UUID validation/repair, and conservative prop/auxiliary visibility.
These changes are maintained in this repository and are not a release of
the original OpenYSM implementation.

Algorithm and dependency attribution

The YSM-modified CityHash64 implementation derives from the CityHash
algorithm by Google. Its retained MIT notice is in CityHash-MIT.txt.
The XChaCha20 lineage includes Bryan Hawkins (BSD-3-Clause), Daniel J.
Bernstein's public-domain ChaCha work and modified libsodium functions
by Frank Denis (ISC). Both the original xchacha20 LICENSE and NOTICE are
retained, including the ISC terms and copyright notice.
Custom YSM Zstandard handling retains the upstream Zstandard BSD notice.

Runtime dependencies include Gson and Error Prone annotations (Apache-2.0),
TwelveMonkeys ImageIO/common modules (BSD-3-Clause), zstd-jni (BSD-2-Clause)
and its bundled native Zstandard (BSD-3-Clause option). JetBrains annotations
are compile-only. Their source attributions and full license terms are
retained under META-INF/licenses. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md provides versions,
sources and distribution instructions. Test and build tooling have their
own licenses as recorded there.

The bundled native Zstandard includes its adapted xxHash implementation.
